in addition to the mass mandate clark  county is renewing its focus on getting  everybody vaccinated this weekend they  brainstorm more and more ways to get  shots in arms  kate houston breaking down how the  mandate impacted vaccination rates and  some potential opportunities for clinics  yes bryan clark county chairwoman  marilyn kirkpatrick says this is an all  hands on deck situation  given the rise in cases and the fast  spreading delta variant  commissioners are trying to get creative  in where they provide additional clinics  right now they're really trying to reach  18 to 40 year olds  which kirkpatrick says have taken the  brunt of the delta variant  they're also trying to find ideal clinic  hours for those who work 12 to 14 hours  a day  many days a week kirkpatrick says there  could be more clinics in malls  car washes job sites and hard hit zip  codes  over the weekend there was a line at the  galleria mall vaccination clinic which  kirkpatrick says was encouraging  some think the mask mandate could  influence even more people to get the  vaccine  it definitely should encourage people to  go back and get vaccinated  especially because i know a lot of  people were feeling good about not  having to wear a mask you know  everything was lifted  so that little bit of freedom that we  had you know is being taken away so i'm  pretty sure people are going to start  getting more  vaccinated and stuff clark county hopes  more people can get the vaccine in the  next few weeks ahead of the new school  year and flu season  kirkpatrick says the delta variant and  the common cold have similar symptoms  and they don't want any further spread  and as students prepare to head back to  class the health district is offering  mandatory vaccines and the covenant 19  vaccine at schools across the valley  for a complete list you can head to our  website 8newsnow.com
 

